<wpt lat="44.092110" lon="10.490610"><name>DZC Sommocolonia — Lieutenant Fox memorial</name><desc>Tour day 12

In this Garfagnana hill village about 70 soldiers of the African-American 92nd 'Buffalo' Division and 25 Italian partisans were overrun on 26 December 1944. Lieutenant John Fox called artillery fire onto his own position to cover the withdrawal and was killed; his Medal of Honor came only in 1997.

The Memory Park at the ruined tower opposite the parish church, a 10-minute walk from the lower car park.

Accuracy: Documented site.

Guide: https://dzcharlie.com/into-europe/

