<wpt lat="44.312330" lon="11.196340"><name>DZC Monte Sole Historical Park</name><desc>Marzabotto

A regional park created in 1989 on the massif where about 770 civilians were killed between 29 September and 5 October 1944. Marked paths link the ruined churches, hamlets and cemeteries of Casaglia, San Martino, Caprara and Cerpiano. The Scuola di Pace Monte Sole and the Il Poggiolo visitor centre run guided visits and education programmes.

Allow: 1 hr 30 min – half day

Guide: https://dzcharlie.com/into-europe/

